# Copy to .dev.vars for local development. NEVER commit the real file.
#
# KEEP THIS FILE SHORT. Cloudflare's "Deploy to Cloudflare" button turns every
# key here into a prompt on the install page, so each line is one more box a
# shopkeeper has to fill before their shop exists. Only things that are (a) a
# genuine secret and (b) answerable on day one belong here. Everything else is
# a setting in the database, editable later in the admin, or a `var` in
# wrangler.jsonc.

# --- First-run protection -----------------------------------------------------
# A freshly deployed shop has no admin password, and the storefront is publicly
# reachable the instant the deploy finishes — before anyone reaches the setup
# wizard. This token is what closes that window: /admin/setup refuses to run
# without it. Invent any long random string; you need it once.
ADMIN_SETUP_TOKEN=

# Signs admin sessions. Any long random string, different from the one above.
#
# Not the cart. The cart's signing key is generated into the database on first
# use, because a forged cart can only affect the forger and prices are always
# re-read from the catalogue. An admin session is a real authorisation
# boundary, so its key is a secret you hold.
SESSION_SECRET=

# --- Everything else is configured in the admin, not here ---------------------
#
# Carrier API token         Admin > Delivery, once you have an account.
# Outbound email API key    Admin > Email. Order emails queue until it is set.
# From/reply-to addresses    Admin > Email — not secrets, and they change.
# UPI VPA and payee name     Admin > Getting paid. Public by nature.
# Alert address              Admin > Email.
#
# Set them here too only if you prefer secrets over settings for the API keys;
# the admin reads the setting first and falls back to the environment.
# DELHIVERY_TOKEN=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
